WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:02.835
-Guys, the big story is
that today President Trump met

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:06.338
with Russian President
Vladimir Putin in Finland.

00:00:06.338 --> 00:00:07.740
Trump was pretty nervous.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.675
So which makes sense,
because most people are nervous

00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:11.176
when meeting their boss.

00:00:11.176 --> 00:00:17.517
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:21.353
They met one-on-one, and the
meeting lasted for two hours --

00:00:21.353 --> 00:00:23.756
or about one hour and 58 minutes
longer than his meeting

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:26.492
with Stormy Daniels.
And just so you know --

00:00:26.492 --> 00:00:27.626
Put it in perspective --

00:00:27.626 --> 00:00:29.762
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:32.632
But it was the first time Trump
and Putin had met one-on-one

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.133
behind closed doors.

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:36.436
And this is very interesting,
Trump actually released a video

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:39.339
to describe how excited he was
to be alone with Putin.

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:40.873
Watch this.

00:00:40.873 --> 00:00:43.543
-I think we're alone now.

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:48.114 line:0%
There doesn't seem
to be anyone around.

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:50.883
And I think we're alone now.

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:54.988 line:0%
The beating of our hearts is the
only sound.

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:56.222
-Yeah.

00:00:56.222 --> 00:01:00.226
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:04.430
Well, according to experts,
Trump and Putin had a lot

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:06.132
to negotiate in their meeting.

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:08.134
Trump says the
negotiations went great.

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:09.969
Putin now controls New York
and California.

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:13.372
And in exchange,
Trump got three magic beans.

00:01:13.372 --> 00:01:14.874
So it's very, very --

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.042
[ As Trump ]
"Who knows what they do.

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:17.877
I don't know.

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:19.211
Embarrassing."

00:01:19.211 --> 00:01:20.647
[ Normal voice ] Actually,
at the end of the meeting,

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:24.216
Trump and Putin didn't sign
any formal deal or agreement,

00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:25.952
mainly because they both spent
the whole time trying

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:28.454
to make sure the other guy
wasn't Sacha Baron Cohen.

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:31.490
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:33.826
[ As Trump ] "Are you real?"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.826 --> 00:01:35.662
[ Normal voice ] But after their
time together, Putin did say

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:37.530
that the meeting went very well.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.565
In fact, it went so well that
Putin said he might make Trump

00:01:39.565 --> 00:01:41.200
President for
another four years.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.436
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:46.172
-Nice of him.
-He said that.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:48.174
A lot of people
are talking about this.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.176
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:52.511
Trump and Putin also held
a press conference

00:01:52.511 --> 00:01:54.681
where Trump actually defended
Putin and seemed to side

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:57.516
with Russia over his own
intelligence agencies.

00:01:57.516 --> 00:01:58.918
Check out what
he said about 2016.

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:01.086 line:0%
-All I can do is ask the
question.

00:02:01.086 --> 00:02:03.022 line:0%
My people came to me.

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:05.291 line:0%
Dan Coats came to me
and some others.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.393 line:0%
They said, they think it's
Russia.

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:12.398 line:0%
I have President Putin.
He just said it's not Russia.

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:15.735 line:0%
I will say this, I don't see
any reason why it would be.

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:17.703
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.703 --> 00:02:20.506
-Well, sure, if Putin told you,
it must be true.

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:22.074
It's like, [ As Trump ]
"Good enough for me.

00:02:22.074 --> 00:02:23.375
My people --"

00:02:23.375 --> 00:02:25.344
[ Normal voice ] What?
[ Applause ]

00:02:25.344 --> 00:02:28.948
But after the press conference,
CNN, MSNBC, and even Fox News

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:31.083
slammed Trump
for his performance.

00:02:31.083 --> 00:02:33.552
Trump said he shouldn't jump
to any conclusions until we hear

00:02:33.552 --> 00:02:37.223
what Cartoon Network has to say.
Then we know it's bad.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:39.625
[ Applause ]

00:02:39.625 --> 00:02:41.693
But, it wasn't all business
at the meeting.

00:02:41.693 --> 00:02:43.663
When he first sat down
with Putin, Trump talked about

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:45.931
the World Cup.
He sounded like a real expert.

00:02:45.931 --> 00:02:46.966
Listen to this.

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:53.006 line:0%
[ Camera shutters clicking ]

00:02:56.709 --> 00:03:01.214
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:02.781
[ As Trump ]
"Soccer -- It's like foosball,

00:03:02.781 --> 00:03:05.617
but with actual people.
Just with actual people."

00:03:05.617 --> 00:03:08.954
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:08.954 --> 00:03:10.590
[ Normal voice ]
Then he said, [ As Trump ]
"And American football

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.659
is the one where I yell at all
the players on Twitter.

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:14.259
That's what we call
it in America."

00:03:14.259 --> 00:03:15.995
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:17.430
[ Normal voice ] At the end
of their press conference,

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.598
Putin actually gave Trump
a soccer ball.

00:03:19.598 --> 00:03:21.467
Take a look at what Trump did
with it, watch this.

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.636 line:0%
-Speaking of the football,
actually.

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:25.772 line:0%
-[ Speaking Russian]

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:28.207 line:0%
-Mr. President, I'll give
this ball to you,

00:03:28.207 --> 00:03:30.108 line:0%
and now the ball is
in your court.

00:03:30.108 --> 00:03:32.044 line:0%
-[ Speaking Russian ]

00:03:32.044 --> 00:03:36.182 line:0%
-That's very nice.
In fact, Melania, here you go.

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:43.289
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:45.458
-That's also how he gave Melania
her engagement ring.

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:47.993
[ As Trump ] "Here,
just pick it up.

00:03:47.993 --> 00:03:49.062
Take it out, take it out."

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:52.164
[ Applause ]

00:03:52.164 --> 00:03:53.666
[ Normal voice ] Putin was like,
[ As Putin ] "Be careful.

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:58.070
There's expensive recording
device inside soccer ball.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:01.340
So speak into
the little nozzle when you --"

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:04.010
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.544
[ Normal voice ] Speaking
of soccer, this weekend,

00:04:05.544 --> 00:04:08.247
France won the World Cup
and they were led by

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:12.885
a 19-year-old prodigy
named Kylian Mbappe, yep.

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:14.620
After the game,
Mbappe said winning

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.856
the World Cup totally makes up
for being named after

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:17.923
a Hanson song.

00:04:17.923 --> 00:04:21.727
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:21.727 --> 00:04:23.763
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:27.533
♪ Mmm-bop, mmm-ma,
mmm-ma, mmm-bop ♪

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:30.269
♪ Mmm-bop, mmm ♪

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:31.270
I know you feel it.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:32.571
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.571 --> 00:04:34.807
Oh, and before he met Putin,
Trump was in the U.K.

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:37.276
where he met Queen Elizabeth.
Did you see that?

00:04:37.276 --> 00:04:39.878
It got off to a bumpy start
when the first thing Trump told

00:04:39.878 --> 00:04:41.213
the Queen was that
he knows all the words

00:04:41.213 --> 00:04:42.481
to "Bohemian Rhapsody."

00:04:42.481 --> 00:04:46.185
He's like, [ As Trump ]
"Can you do the fandango?

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:48.321
I do fandango. Mbappe."

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:50.556
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:52.158
[ Normal voice ] You see this?
When Trump met with the Queen,

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:54.126
they went to view
the Royal Guards.

00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:56.695
And he got a little confused
about where to position himself.

00:04:56.695 --> 00:04:57.697
Check this out.

00:04:57.697 --> 00:05:05.738 line:0%
[ Band playing ]

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:10.209 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:13.379
Oh, my goodness.

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:17.483
-Oh, come on!
What?

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:20.619
-Trump walks like every single
tourist in Times Square.

00:05:20.619 --> 00:05:31.497
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:33.232
[ As Trump ] "There's a lot
of M&amp;Ms in that store.

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:36.068
Take a picture.
That's a lot of M&amp;Ms."

00:05:36.068 --> 00:05:38.938
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:40.305
[ Normal voice ] All right.
Some good news here --

00:05:40.305 --> 00:05:42.642
the 12 boys who were rescued
from a cave in Thailand

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:44.677
last week are
about to be released.

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:47.746
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:47.746 --> 00:05:50.416
They're about to be released
from the hospital.

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:53.185
They said the first thing
they want to eat is KFC.

00:05:53.185 --> 00:05:54.220
[ Light laughter ]

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.621
Then their doctor is
like, "Dear God,

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:57.022
haven't your bodies
been through enough?

00:05:57.022 --> 00:05:59.291
I mean, good, please.

00:05:59.291 --> 00:06:00.960
What are you doing?"

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:04.062
And finally, I heard that you
can now buy high-heeled Crocs

00:06:04.062 --> 00:06:05.331
on Amazon.

00:06:05.331 --> 00:06:06.732
[ Light laughter ]

00:06:06.732 --> 00:06:08.333
Take a look at these.

00:06:08.333 --> 00:06:09.835
Yep.

00:06:09.835 --> 00:06:12.071
They're great for when you want
say, "I have somewhere to go

00:06:12.071 --> 00:06:13.740
and nowhere to go
at the same time."

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.207
You guys, we have
a great show tonight.

00:06:15.207 --> 00:06:16.209
Give it up for The Roots!

